  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_LO2_NetworkServices_Q03
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: Why is the server's preferred DNS server set to 127.0.0.1?
  choices:
  - It is hosting DNS itself, so it resolves names by asking itself
  - 127.0.0.1 is the fastest DNS server available
  - It stops the server from reaching the internet
  - Domain controllers are not allowed to use a real DNS address
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  points: 10
  explanation: The loopback address points the machine at its own DNS service. Pointing
    it elsewhere would leave a domain controller unable to resolve its own domain.
